// Title: Obfuscated PowerShell MSI Install via WindowsInstaller COM
// Sigma ID: 63cb4379-81f0-423c-8904-dc3c0d932b71
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Meroujan Antonyan (vx3r)
// Date: 2025-05-27 | Modified: 2026-11-06
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1027.010, T1218.007, execution, T1059.001
// Description: Detects the execution of obfuscated PowerShell commands that attempt to install MSI packages via
//   the Windows Installer COM object (`WindowsInstaller.Installer`). The technique involves
//   manipulating strings to hide functionality, such as constructing class names using string
//   insertion (e.g., 'indowsInstaller.Installer'.Insert(0,'W')) and correcting malformed URLs (e.g.,
//   converting 'htps://' to 'https://') at runtime. This behavior is commonly associated with
//   malware loaders or droppers that aim to bypass static detection by hiding intent in runtime-
//   generated strings and using legitimate tools for code execution. The use of `InstallProduct` and
//   COM object creation, particularly combined with hidden window execution and suppressed UI,
//   indicates an attempt to install software (likely malicious) without user interaction.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://informationsecuritybuzz.com/the-real-danger-behind-a-simple-windows-shortcut/
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/threat-intelligence/intelligence-insights-may-2025/
//   - https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/f9710b0ba4de5fa0e7ec27da462d4d2fc6838eba83a19f23f6617a466bbad457
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/7490edb4783550895f8ac7b1ff297eaa8fda0d2a/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_comobject_msi.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\powershell_ise.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe") or (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName in~ ("PowerShell_ISE.EXE", "PowerShell.EXE", "pwsh.dll"))) and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-ComObject" and ProcessCommandLine contains "InstallProduct(" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".Insert(" and ProcessCommandLine contains "UILevel")
